{
  "video": {
    "id": "SxaoWJ2gkzc",
    "title": "Photosynthesis | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SxaoWJ2gkzc",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 1022,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 254,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 11.293,
      "end": 12.23,
      "duration": 0.937,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 12.23,
      "end": 16.37,
      "duration": 4.14,
      "text": "So I need to move on a little bit now, and I want to talk"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 16.37,
      "end": 24.54,
      "duration": 8.17,
      "text": "about in fact, the earlier way that nature developed to make"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 24.54,
      "end": 27.93,
      "duration": 3.39,
      "text": "energy using proton gradients."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 27.93,
      "end": 30.94,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "And this part actually preceded the development of"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 30.94,
      "end": 32.7,
      "duration": 1.76,
      "text": "respiration as you'll see."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 32.7,
      "end": 37.93,
      "duration": 5.23,
      "text": "It's what I somewhat flippantly refer to as"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 37.93,
      "end": 41.97,
      "duration": 4.04,
      "text": "photosynthesis release 1."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 41.97,
      "end": 44.06,
      "duration": 2.09,
      "text": "In my first lecture, when I was giving"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 44.06,
      "end": 49.18,
      "duration": 5.12,
      "text": "you a sketch of evolution."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 49.18,
      "end": 52.48,
      "duration": 3.3,
      "text": "Who knows, I mean these are very rough numbers, but may"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 52.48,
      "end": 57.33,
      "duration": 4.85,
      "text": "have evolved about $3.4 billion years ago and early"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 57.33,
      "end": 60.715,
      "duration": 3.385,
      "text": "life had begun to exhaust this sea of chemicals"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 60.715,
      "end": 62.97,
      "duration": 2.255,
      "text": "that had been produced."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 62.97,
      "end": 68.63,
      "duration": 5.66,
      "text": "And it's known as cyclic photophosphorylation."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 77.4,
      "end": 80.69,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "And it's a way of taking the energy in"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 80.69,
      "end": 86.47,
      "duration": 5.78,
      "text": "sunlight and making ATP."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 86.47,
      "end": 90.54,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "So whatever organism figured this out, this was"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 90.54,
      "end": 91.59,
      "duration": 1.05,
      "text": "a really big deal."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 91.59,
      "end": 95.1,
      "duration": 3.51,
      "text": "Because now instead of having to use the sort of natural"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 95.1,
      "end": 99.35,
      "duration": 4.25,
      "text": "reserves like the way the food around is a depleting resource"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 99.35,
      "end": 101.95,
      "duration": 2.6,
      "text": "just like our petroleum reserves, this was able to"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 101.95,
      "end": 104.78,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "take the abundantly-available sunlight and"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 104.78,
      "end": 107.28,
      "duration": 2.5,
      "text": "use it to make energy."
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 107.28,
      "end": 109.84,
      "duration": 2.56,
      "text": "So that's the principle."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 109.84,
      "end": 113.59,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "It uses the energy in sunlight, and the way it does"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 113.59,
      "end": 122.58,
      "duration": 8.99,
      "text": "it, is it uses the sunlight to establish a proton gradient"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 122.58,
      "end": 126.29,
      "duration": 3.71,
      "text": "just as we've been discussing earlier, and then uses"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 126.29,
      "end": 131.16,
      "duration": 4.87,
      "text": "that to make ATP."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 131.16,
      "end": 138.63,
      "duration": 7.47,
      "text": "And there's a special molecule that's involved in absorbing"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 138.63,
      "end": 141.62,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "the energy from the sunlight."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 141.62,
      "end": 144.56,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "We've all heard it I'm sure, chlorophyll."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 144.56,
      "end": 146.87,
      "duration": 2.31,
      "text": "There are a couple of two major"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 146.87,
      "end": 149.4,
      "duration": 2.53,
      "text": "variants of this molecule."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 149.4,
      "end": 152.81,
      "duration": 3.41,
      "text": "Here's one of them, chlorophyll a, and you don't"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 152.81,
      "end": 154.15,
      "duration": 1.34,
      "text": "have to memorize the structure."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 154.15,
      "end": 155.85,
      "duration": 1.7,
      "text": "But I want you to notice a couple of things."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 155.85,
      "end": 160.8,
      "duration": 4.95,
      "text": "One is there's a metal in the middle, a magnesium, and then"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 160.8,
      "end": 169.8,
      "duration": 9.0,
      "text": "it's coordinated with the cyclic ring system."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 169.8,
      "end": 172.78,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "And notice all the conjugated double bonds."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 172.78,
      "end": 178.09,
      "duration": 5.31,
      "text": "So this chlorophyll was tuned to absorb energy from the"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 178.09,
      "end": 179.845,
      "duration": 1.755,
      "text": "visible range of sunlight."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 179.845,
      "end": 183.51,
      "duration": 3.665,
      "text": "And when it absorbs a photon of energy, it kicks an"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 183.51,
      "end": 186.45,
      "duration": 2.94,
      "text": "electron up to a higher orbital."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 186.45,
      "end": 189.94,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "And if the electron's in a higher orbital, it's more"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 189.94,
      "end": 192.13,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "easily lost."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 192.13,
      "end": 193.81,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "And this has a consequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 193.81,
      "end": 200.02,
      "duration": 6.21,
      "text": "So the way this system works is you have a molecule of"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 200.02,
      "end": 203.58,
      "duration": 3.56,
      "text": "chlorophyll, that's what I'm abbreviating here."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 203.58,
      "end": 206.42,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "Oh, let me tell you something else too."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 206.42,
      "end": 209.26,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "It's more sophisticated than this."
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 209.26,
      "end": 212.85,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "So this is the molecule that absorbs a particular"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 212.85,
      "end": 214.65,
      "duration": 1.8,
      "text": "wavelength from sunlight."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 214.65,
      "end": 220.91,
      "duration": 6.26,
      "text": "But this is embedded in a multi-protein structure that"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 220.91,
      "end": 226.33,
      "duration": 5.42,
      "text": "has a bunch of other molecules that absorb at different"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 226.33,
      "end": 229.77,
      "duration": 3.44,
      "text": "wavelengths and then funnel that energy down to the one"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 229.77,
      "end": 231.81,
      "duration": 2.04,
      "text": "the chlorophyll comes in."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 231.81,
      "end": 235.56,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "So in fact, the whole thing is like a big antenna that's able"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 235.56,
      "end": 238.42,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "to absorb quite a bit of energy from different"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 238.42,
      "end": 241.31,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "wavelengths in sunlight and get it down to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 241.31,
      "end": 242.47,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "chlorophyll."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 242.47,
      "end": 250.51,
      "duration": 8.04,
      "text": "When the chlorophyll absorbs energy, it goes up to an"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 250.51,
      "end": 252.67,
      "duration": 2.16,
      "text": "excited state."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 252.67,
      "end": 254.91,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "And as I said, now that the electron's in a higher"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 254.91,
      "end": 257.64,
      "duration": 2.73,
      "text": "orbital, it's lost more easily."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 257.64,
      "end": 260.649,
      "duration": 3.009,
      "text": "So this has become a better reducing agent."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 260.649,
      "end": 263.67,
      "duration": 3.021,
      "text": "It's able to give its electrons to things that it"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 263.67,
      "end": 266.45,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "couldn't do down in this energy state."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 266.45,
      "end": 269.13,
      "duration": 2.68,
      "text": "So we come down one of these thermodynamic hills that"
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 269.13,
      "end": 271.85,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "you're hopefully starting to get used to where it comes"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 271.85,
      "end": 276.18,
      "duration": 4.33,
      "text": "down in little hops to a carrier that has this set"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 276.18,
      "end": 279.58,
      "duration": 3.4,
      "text": "level of energy, down, free energy, down."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 283.72,
      "end": 287.65,
      "duration": 3.93,
      "text": "And similarly, to the principle that we talked about"
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 287.65,
      "end": 294.21,
      "duration": 6.56,
      "text": "in respiration, a proton is pumped from what I'm going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 294.21,
      "end": 300.38,
      "duration": 6.17,
      "text": "say, in this case, I'll show you what I mean, but I'll say"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 300.38,
      "end": 306.14,
      "duration": 5.76,
      "text": "from a proton that's out to a proton that's in."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 306.14,
      "end": 311.31,
      "duration": 5.17,
      "text": "And by doing that, it establishes a proton gradient,"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 311.31,
      "end": 313.23,
      "duration": 1.92,
      "text": "and that gives rise to ATP."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 317.08,
      "end": 320.74,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "At the end of this cycle, we have this chlorophyll minus"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 320.74,
      "end": 322.17,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "the electrons."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 322.17,
      "end": 324.07,
      "duration": 1.9,
      "text": "These come, flow back."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 324.07,
      "end": 328.61,
      "duration": 4.54,
      "text": "That's why it's called cyclic photophosphorylation."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 328.61,
      "end": 333.33,
      "duration": 4.72,
      "text": "The electrons go through these carriers, and then they return"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 333.33,
      "end": 334.76,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "to chlorophyll."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 334.76,
      "end": 336.645,
      "duration": 1.885,
      "text": "So wonderful system."
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 343.5,
      "end": 345.67,
      "duration": 2.17,
      "text": "I seemed to have accidentally advanced this."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 345.67,
      "end": 346.26,
      "duration": 0.59,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 346.26,
      "end": 351.55,
      "duration": 5.29,
      "text": "There are still bacteria around that run this system."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 351.55,
      "end": 356.17,
      "duration": 4.62,
      "text": "So if you remember, we talked about biosynthesis, the need"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 356.17,
      "end": 356.625,
      "duration": 0.455,
      "text": "for energy."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 356.625,
      "end": 357.39,
      "duration": 0.765,
      "text": "Well, here we are."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 357.39,
      "end": 358.36,
      "duration": 0.97,
      "text": "We got ATP."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 358.36,
      "end": 360.43,
      "duration": 2.07,
      "text": "But there is something else hopefully you now appreciate"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 360.43,
      "end": 366.4,
      "duration": 5.97,
      "text": "in that is that ATP is not enough to take carbon dioxide"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 366.4,
      "end": 369.03,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "and make it into sugars or carbon compounds."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 369.03,
      "end": 371.19,
      "duration": 2.16,
      "text": "We need a source of reducing power as well."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 371.19,
      "end": 374.46,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "Because remember, carbon dioxide is the most oxidized"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 374.46,
      "end": 376.14,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "form of carbon."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 376.14,
      "end": 381.08,
      "duration": 4.94,
      "text": "So these early organism solved it by making reducing power"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 381.08,
      "end": 384.45,
      "duration": 3.37,
      "text": "from another source."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 384.45,
      "end": 389.26,
      "duration": 4.81,
      "text": "Many of them used hydrogen sulfide as a source, and they"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 389.26,
      "end": 392.15,
      "duration": 2.89,
      "text": "used NADP plus."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 392.15,
      "end": 396.09,
      "duration": 3.94,
      "text": "Now, this is a minor variation of NADH."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 396.09,
      "end": 398.37,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "It's got one more phosphate on it."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 398.37,
      "end": 400.73,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "You can look it up in your book."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 400.73,
      "end": 405.44,
      "duration": 4.71,
      "text": "This variant of NAD is used preferentially for"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 405.44,
      "end": 406.88,
      "duration": 1.44,
      "text": "biosynthetic purposes."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 406.88,
      "end": 410.66,
      "duration": 3.78,
      "text": "But everything I've told you about NAD in terms of banking"
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 410.66,
      "end": 412.66,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "electrons applies here."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 412.66,
      "end": 418.5,
      "duration": 5.84,
      "text": "So the electrons from here are grabbed."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 418.5,
      "end": 426.64,
      "duration": 8.14,
      "text": "The cell makes NADPH, which you can use as reducing power"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 426.64,
      "end": 427.89,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "for biosynthesis."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 430.66,
      "end": 434.32,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "You get elemental sulfur and hydrogen ions."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 434.32,
      "end": 441.16,
      "duration": 6.84,
      "text": "So this process an organism that used this kind of"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 441.16,
      "end": 444.68,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "photophosphorylation to make ATP would get its reducing"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 444.68,
      "end": 447.93,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "power through a process something like this."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 447.93,
      "end": 452.5,
      "duration": 4.57,
      "text": "And then it could make sugars, and then from that point on,"
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 452.5,
      "end": 455.17,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "they can be used to make all the other"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 455.17,
      "end": 456.86,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "molecules that you need."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 456.86,
      "end": 460.17,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "The key thing is to get from the carbon dioxide down into a"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 460.17,
      "end": 463.28,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "more reduced form of carbon."
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 463.28,
      "end": 468.05,
      "duration": 4.77,
      "text": "So that works pretty well."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 468.05,
      "end": 473.58,
      "duration": 5.53,
      "text": "However, a better system came up involved in evolution."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 473.58,
      "end": 480.18,
      "duration": 6.6,
      "text": "This was the one I again somewhat flippantly called"
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 480.18,
      "end": 486.69,
      "duration": 6.51,
      "text": "photosynthesis release 2, when I was talking."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 486.69,
      "end": 494.38,
      "duration": 7.69,
      "text": "This is known as, probably came up who knows again but"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 494.38,
      "end": 507.9,
      "duration": 13.52,
      "text": "maybe 3 billion years ago, and it's known as noncyclic"
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 507.9,
      "end": 509.53,
      "duration": 1.63,
      "text": "photophosphorylation."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 509.53,
      "end": 512.75,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "And what's important about this system and why it's an"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 512.75,
      "end": 517.27,
      "duration": 4.52,
      "text": "improvement over the other, is it uses the energy in sunlight"
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 517.27,
      "end": 521.82,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "to make ATP just as we've learned, but it also uses the"
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 521.82,
      "end": 527.18,
      "duration": 5.36,
      "text": "energy in sunlight to make NADPH."
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 527.18,
      "end": 532.01,
      "duration": 4.83,
      "text": "So in other words, this second version gives the cell simply"
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 532.01,
      "end": 535.33,
      "duration": 3.32,
      "text": "from the energy in sunlight everything it needs to take"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 535.33,
      "end": 540.16,
      "duration": 4.83,
      "text": "carbon dioxide and make it into organic compounds."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 540.16,
      "end": 543.19,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "And it's a pretty cool system evolutionarily."
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 543.19,
      "end": 547.49,
      "duration": 4.3,
      "text": "It's built on the older one, the first arising one."
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 547.49,
      "end": 551.35,
      "duration": 3.86,
      "text": "You'll still see the elements of the present but with a new"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 551.35,
      "end": 556.09,
      "duration": 4.74,
      "text": "variation added in, very much the way we do design when"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 556.09,
      "end": 556.795,
      "duration": 0.705,
      "text": "you're doing engineering."
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 556.795,
      "end": 559.77,
      "duration": 2.975,
      "text": "You get something that's working, and you can use that"
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 559.77,
      "end": 562.82,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "as a basis to move to a new and improved version."
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 562.82,
      "end": 564.925,
      "duration": 2.105,
      "text": "And naturally, if you get a new and improved version, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 564.925,
      "end": 567.27,
      "duration": 2.345,
      "text": "you get a little advantage over your neighbors, natural"
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 567.27,
      "end": 572.76,
      "duration": 5.49,
      "text": "selection makes sure that that better system gets"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 572.76,
      "end": 574.16,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "established."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 574.16,
      "end": 577.11,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "So here's here how this noncyclic"
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 577.11,
      "end": 578.89,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "photophosphorylation starts."
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 578.89,
      "end": 585.535,
      "duration": 6.645,
      "text": "We take a chlorophyll and it absorbs the quantum of energy,"
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 585.535,
      "end": 590.65,
      "duration": 5.115,
      "text": "and it kicks itself up to an excited state."
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 590.65,
      "end": 596.23,
      "duration": 5.58,
      "text": "The chlorophyll, as before, electrons come down,"
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 596.23,
      "end": 598.76,
      "duration": 2.53,
      "text": "energetically downhill and remember that theme."
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 598.76,
      "end": 603.15,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "I keep saying that's at least thermodynamic properties."
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 603.15,
      "end": 604.91,
      "duration": 1.76,
      "text": "If we think about free energy, it doesn't matter"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 604.91,
      "end": 605.92,
      "duration": 1.01,
      "text": "what path you take."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 605.92,
      "end": 609.28,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "Whether you come shooting right down or you come down"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 609.28,
      "end": 612.12,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "through it, you get the same energy back."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 612.12,
      "end": 614.12,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "What's amazing about the system, if it didn't have all"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 614.12,
      "end": 616.79,
      "duration": 2.67,
      "text": "this extra apparatus, you'd kick up the electron, and then"
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 616.79,
      "end": 618.88,
      "duration": 2.09,
      "text": "it would just come right back and you'd get a little"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 618.88,
      "end": 620.13,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "radiated, a little energy given off."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 620.13,
      "end": 621.48,
      "duration": 1.35,
      "text": "We wouldn't have accomplished anything."
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 621.48,
      "end": 625.68,
      "duration": 4.2,
      "text": "And what's terrific about this photophosphorylation system,"
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 625.68,
      "end": 628.78,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "it's able to capture the energy that's in that excited"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 628.78,
      "end": 629.78,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "text": "chlorophyll."
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 629.78,
      "end": 635.17,
      "duration": 5.39,
      "text": "So at this point, and as it's coming down as I said, we have"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 635.17,
      "end": 640.09,
      "duration": 4.92,
      "text": "H plus going from H plus, H plus in."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 640.09,
      "end": 643.09,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "I'll give you a picture of what I mean by that."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 643.09,
      "end": 646.38,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "Then we're getting ATP made."
    },
    {
      "index": 169,
      "start": 646.38,
      "end": 650.92,
      "duration": 4.54,
      "text": "So this time the difference is instead of the electrons going"
    },
    {
      "index": 170,
      "start": 650.92,
      "end": 654.94,
      "duration": 4.02,
      "text": "back to that chlorophyll, it was missing its electrons, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 171,
      "start": 654.94,
      "end": 660.71,
      "duration": 5.77,
      "text": "electrons, instead, go to a chlorophyll, which is at a"
    },
    {
      "index": 172,
      "start": 660.71,
      "end": 664.0,
      "duration": 3.29,
      "text": "somewhat higher energy level than the first one."
    },
    {
      "index": 173,
      "start": 664.0,
      "end": 669.295,
      "duration": 5.295,
      "text": "And it has just absorbed quantum of energy, and it's"
    },
    {
      "index": 174,
      "start": 669.295,
      "end": 676.72,
      "duration": 7.425,
      "text": "kicked itself up to an even more excited state."
    },
    {
      "index": 175,
      "start": 676.72,
      "end": 682.39,
      "duration": 5.67,
      "text": "And these electrons from this system come on and fill up"
    },
    {
      "index": 176,
      "start": 682.39,
      "end": 684.77,
      "duration": 2.38,
      "text": "this chlorophyll."
    },
    {
      "index": 177,
      "start": 684.77,
      "end": 693.495,
      "duration": 8.725,
      "text": "So this one over here is called photosystem II."
    },
    {
      "index": 178,
      "start": 693.495,
      "end": 696.53,
      "duration": 3.035,
      "text": "And the term used in the field to describe what I'm about to"
    },
    {
      "index": 179,
      "start": 696.53,
      "end": 707.65,
      "duration": 11.12,
      "text": "tell you here is now called photosystem I."
    },
    {
      "index": 180,
      "start": 707.65,
      "end": 714.55,
      "duration": 6.9,
      "text": "So what we have now from this system is an excited molecule,"
    },
    {
      "index": 181,
      "start": 714.55,
      "end": 719.19,
      "duration": 4.64,
      "text": "chlorophyll, that's even more excited than we were before."
    },
    {
      "index": 182,
      "start": 719.19,
      "end": 723.0,
      "duration": 3.81,
      "text": "And so it's even more able to give off its electrons."
    },
    {
      "index": 183,
      "start": 723.0,
      "end": 724.75,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "It has more reducing power."
    },
    {
      "index": 184,
      "start": 724.75,
      "end": 727.24,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "In fact, it has enough reducing power that it can"
    },
    {
      "index": 185,
      "start": 727.24,
      "end": 729.44,
      "duration": 2.2,
      "text": "reduce NADP."
    },
    {
      "index": 186,
      "start": 729.44,
      "end": 742.03,
      "duration": 12.59,
      "text": "So NADP plus, electrons coming downhill, you get NADPH."
    },
    {
      "index": 187,
      "start": 745.69,
      "end": 752.0,
      "duration": 6.31,
      "text": "So here we are, reducing power made by using the energy in"
    },
    {
      "index": 188,
      "start": 752.0,
      "end": 758.66,
      "duration": 6.66,
      "text": "sunlight, ATP made using the energy in sunlight."
    },
    {
      "index": 189,
      "start": 758.66,
      "end": 763.3,
      "duration": 4.64,
      "text": "So by just using this noncyclic photophosphorylation"
    },
    {
      "index": 190,
      "start": 763.3,
      "end": 768.93,
      "duration": 5.63,
      "text": "system, the cell's got what it needs to take carbon dioxide"
    },
    {
      "index": 191,
      "start": 768.93,
      "end": 771.74,
      "duration": 2.81,
      "text": "and put it through a sequence of reactions that will let it"
    },
    {
      "index": 192,
      "start": 771.74,
      "end": 773.6,
      "duration": 1.86,
      "text": "make sugars and other things."
    },
    {
      "index": 193,
      "start": 773.6,
      "end": 776.02,
      "duration": 2.42,
      "text": "In this course, I don't have enough time to go through the"
    },
    {
      "index": 194,
      "start": 776.02,
      "end": 778.47,
      "duration": 2.45,
      "text": "biosynthetic pathway."
    },
    {
      "index": 195,
      "start": 778.47,
      "end": 779.94,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "It's in your textbooks."
    },
    {
      "index": 196,
      "start": 779.94,
      "end": 782.455,
      "duration": 2.515,
      "text": "You might find it interesting to look at."
    },
    {
      "index": 197,
      "start": 782.455,
      "end": 784.49,
      "duration": 2.035,
      "text": "We're not making a big issue of it in there."
    },
    {
      "index": 198,
      "start": 784.49,
      "end": 787.5,
      "duration": 3.01,
      "text": "But it exists, and you can see that it obviously exists."
    },
    {
      "index": 199,
      "start": 787.5,
      "end": 791.55,
      "duration": 4.05,
      "text": "So there's one more wrinkle here which might be sort of"
    },
    {
      "index": 200,
      "start": 791.55,
      "end": 795.615,
      "duration": 4.065,
      "text": "eerily reminiscent of one of the issue I posed for you when"
    },
    {
      "index": 201,
      "start": 795.615,
      "end": 799.67,
      "duration": 4.055,
      "text": "I asked about whether we could just keep on doing glycolysis."
    },
    {
      "index": 202,
      "start": 799.67,
      "end": 801.24,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "I can't just let the system run."
    },
    {
      "index": 203,
      "start": 804.84,
      "end": 807.8,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "I forgot about something so far."
    },
    {
      "index": 204,
      "start": 807.8,
      "end": 811.63,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "Over here, this guy lost an electron."
    },
    {
      "index": 205,
      "start": 811.63,
      "end": 814.99,
      "duration": 3.36,
      "text": "It can't get it back because the electrons went over there."
    },
    {
      "index": 206,
      "start": 814.99,
      "end": 816.72,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "They have to come from somewhere."
    },
    {
      "index": 207,
      "start": 816.72,
      "end": 820.17,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "Well, the energetics of the system now are such that it"
    },
    {
      "index": 208,
      "start": 820.17,
      "end": 825.515,
      "duration": 5.345,
      "text": "can get electrons from water."
    },
    {
      "index": 209,
      "start": 825.515,
      "end": 828.84,
      "duration": 3.325,
      "text": "And what's left over when you take the electrons from water?"
    },
    {
      "index": 210,
      "start": 828.84,
      "end": 834.04,
      "duration": 5.2,
      "text": "We have half of an oxygen molecule."
    },
    {
      "index": 211,
      "start": 834.04,
      "end": 839.12,
      "duration": 5.08,
      "text": "So here's the class."
    },
    {
      "index": 212,
      "start": 839.12,
      "end": 845.43,
      "duration": 6.31,
      "text": "It's a waste product, if you will, from this very efficient"
    },
    {
      "index": 213,
      "start": 845.43,
      "end": 848.12,
      "duration": 2.69,
      "text": "noncyclic photophosphorylation system, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 214,
      "start": 848.12,
      "end": 849.88,
      "duration": 1.76,
      "text": "it's molecular oxygen."
    },
    {
      "index": 215,
      "start": 849.88,
      "end": 853.02,
      "duration": 3.14,
      "text": "And it was when this system developed that we started to"
    },
    {
      "index": 216,
      "start": 853.02,
      "end": 857.81,
      "duration": 4.79,
      "text": "have oxygen appear in this world."
    },
    {
      "index": 217,
      "start": 857.81,
      "end": 865.26,
      "duration": 7.45,
      "text": "The organelle that carries out photosynthesis, actually, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 218,
      "start": 865.26,
      "end": 870.94,
      "duration": 5.68,
      "text": "first organisms that learned how to do this is called"
    },
    {
      "index": 219,
      "start": 870.94,
      "end": 875.06,
      "duration": 4.12,
      "text": "cyanobacteria, which they sometimes sort of rather"
    },
    {
      "index": 220,
      "start": 875.06,
      "end": 876.6,
      "duration": 1.54,
      "text": "incorrectly call blue-green algae"
    },
    {
      "index": 221,
      "start": 876.6,
      "end": 879.65,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "because they're bacteria."
    },
    {
      "index": 222,
      "start": 879.65,
      "end": 882.71,
      "duration": 3.06,
      "text": "But you see cyanobacteria all the time."
    },
    {
      "index": 223,
      "start": 882.71,
      "end": 885.62,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "And similarly to what happened with the mitochondria, there's"
    },
    {
      "index": 224,
      "start": 885.62,
      "end": 890.15,
      "duration": 4.53,
      "text": "no abundant evidence that the way photosynthesis happens in"
    },
    {
      "index": 225,
      "start": 890.15,
      "end": 896.7,
      "duration": 6.55,
      "text": "plants is a cyanobacterium got trapped somehow inside a early"
    },
    {
      "index": 226,
      "start": 896.7,
      "end": 899.28,
      "duration": 2.58,
      "text": "plant cell, and is now a permanent part"
    },
    {
      "index": 227,
      "start": 899.28,
      "end": 901.55,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "of the plant cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 228,
      "start": 901.55,
      "end": 902.8,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "And it's called a chloroplast."
    },
    {
      "index": 229,
      "start": 906.56,
      "end": 909.16,
      "duration": 2.6,
      "text": "So it's derived from a bacterium."
    },
    {
      "index": 230,
      "start": 909.16,
      "end": 913.4,
      "duration": 4.24,
      "text": "If you see plants are green."
    },
    {
      "index": 231,
      "start": 913.4,
      "end": 920.43,
      "duration": 7.03,
      "text": "If you can look in and see the chloroplast inside, this shows"
    },
    {
      "index": 232,
      "start": 920.43,
      "end": 921.92,
      "duration": 1.49,
      "text": "the chloroplast coming in."
    },
    {
      "index": 233,
      "start": 921.92,
      "end": 923.87,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "And here's their basic structure."
    },
    {
      "index": 234,
      "start": 923.87,
      "end": 927.36,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "They too have a double membrane."
    },
    {
      "index": 235,
      "start": 927.36,
      "end": 929.1,
      "duration": 1.74,
      "text": "They have an outer membrane."
    },
    {
      "index": 236,
      "start": 929.1,
      "end": 930.36,
      "duration": 1.26,
      "text": "They have an inner membrane."
    },
    {
      "index": 237,
      "start": 933.84,
      "end": 938.91,
      "duration": 5.07,
      "text": "They have a part that's called the stroma, and that's"
    },
    {
      "index": 238,
      "start": 938.91,
      "end": 944.38,
      "duration": 5.47,
      "text": "essentially, like the cytoplasm of a normal cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 239,
      "start": 944.38,
      "end": 949.13,
      "duration": 4.75,
      "text": "And they have something in here called a lumen."
    },
    {
      "index": 240,
      "start": 949.13,
      "end": 953.36,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "It's a space, and the membrane that bounds it is a special"
    },
    {
      "index": 241,
      "start": 953.36,
      "end": 959.04,
      "duration": 5.68,
      "text": "membrane called a thylakoid membrane."
    },
    {
      "index": 242,
      "start": 966.58,
      "end": 971.07,
      "duration": 4.49,
      "text": "And that gradient is established by pumping an"
    },
    {
      "index": 243,
      "start": 971.07,
      "end": 977.06,
      "duration": 5.99,
      "text": "electron from the stroma, which I called out, into the"
    },
    {
      "index": 244,
      "start": 977.06,
      "end": 980.19,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "lumen, which I called in."
    },
    {
      "index": 245,
      "start": 980.19,
      "end": 984.54,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "text": "Again, the point is this cell managed to establish a proton"
    },
    {
      "index": 246,
      "start": 984.54,
      "end": 989.09,
      "duration": 4.55,
      "text": "gradient, and it's able to make the chloroplast, able to"
    },
    {
      "index": 247,
      "start": 989.09,
      "end": 993.23,
      "duration": 4.14,
      "text": "establish a protein gradient, and make ATP."
    },
    {
      "index": 248,
      "start": 993.23,
      "end": 998.51,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "And there's a transmission micrograph of a chloroplast."
    },
    {
      "index": 249,
      "start": 998.51,
      "end": 1002.9,
      "duration": 4.39,
      "text": "You can see the thylakoid membranes inside."
    },
    {
      "index": 250,
      "start": 1002.9,
      "end": 1005.83,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "It's not too hard to imagine that that was, in fact, a"
    },
    {
      "index": 251,
      "start": 1005.83,
      "end": 1007.66,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "cyanobacterium that got in there."
    },
    {
      "index": 252,
      "start": 1007.66,
      "end": 1009.98,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "And there's quite a bit of additional evidence that"
    },
    {
      "index": 253,
      "start": 1009.98,
      "end": 1011.23,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "supports that."
    }
  ],
